gs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Fresh and organic for the best flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">crumbled feta cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds tanginess and creaminess</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">milk</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Helps to make the eggs fluffier</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"4\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">butter or olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For cooking and richness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"5\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"6\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"7\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh herbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional: chopped parsley or chives for garnish</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3789-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3789\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Nonstick skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the eggs</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For whisking the eggs</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3789-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3789-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3789\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Crack the Eggs &#8211; Crack the eggs into a bowl. Add a splash of milk, salt, and pepper. Whisk until everything is combined and frothy.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Heat the Skillet &#8211; Heat a tablespoon of butter or olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium heat. Let it warm up until it’s nice and hot.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Pour in the Egg Mixture &#8211; Pour the egg mixture into the skillet. Let it cook undisturbed for 1–2 minutes. Watch as the edges start to set!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Add the Feta &#8211; When the edges begin to set, sprinkle crumbled feta evenly over the surface. It’s time to add that creamy goodness!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Cook Until Set &#8211; Continue cooking until the eggs are mostly set but still slightly runny on top. This keeps them fluffy and delicious.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Fold the Omelette &#8211; Gently fold the omelette in half. Slide it onto a plate with a flourish. You did it!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3789-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Garnish and Serve &#8211; Garnish with fresh herbs if desired. Serve immediately and enjoy your tasty creation!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3789-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>18g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>16g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delightful dishes with these simple ingredients perfect for feta and egg recipe!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Feta-and-Egg-Recipes.webp\" alt=\"A kitchen table displaying fresh ingredients for feta and egg recipes, including eggs, feta cheese, milk, butter, salt, pepper, and fresh herbs.\" class=\"wp-image-3787\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Feta-and-Egg-Recipes.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Feta-and-Egg-Recipes-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 large eggs</strong> – fresh and organic for the best flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup crumbled feta cheese</strong> – adds tanginess and creaminess</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons milk</strong> – helps to make the eggs fluffier</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon butter or olive oil</strong> – for cooking and richness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>black pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>fresh herbs</strong> – optional: chopped parsley or chives for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-feta-and-egg-recipes\"><strong>How to Make Feta and Egg Recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful dish takes about 5 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to cook. Enjoy it fresh off the skillet!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Feta-and-Egg-Recipe-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide for making feta and egg recipes, showcasing the preparation process in a divided image format.\" class=\"wp-image-3788\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Feta-and-Egg-Recipe-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Feta-and-Egg-Recipe-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Crack the Eggs</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Crack the eggs into a bowl. Add a splash of milk, salt, and pepper. Whisk until everything is combined and frothy.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Heat the Skillet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat a tablespoon of butter or olive oil in a nonstick skillet over medium heat. Let it warm up until it’s nice and hot.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Pour in the Egg Mixture</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pour the egg mixture into the skillet. Let it cook undisturbed for 1–2 minutes. Watch as the edges start to set!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add the Feta</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When the edges begin to set, sprinkle crumbled feta evenly over the surface. It’s time to add that creamy goodness!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Cook Until Set</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Continue cooking until the eggs are mostly set but still slightly runny on top. This keeps them fluffy and delicious.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Fold the Omelette</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gently fold the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omelette\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">omelette </a>in half. Slide it onto a plate with a flourish. You did it!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish with fresh herbs if desired. Serve immediately and enjoy your tasty creation!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Breakfast</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Mediterranean</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm and fluffy with fresh herbs!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-feta-and-egg-recipes\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Feta and Egg Recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Opt for crumbled feta for even distribution in your dish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with fresh herbs like dill or parsley for added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cook eggs on low heat for a creamy texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with whole grain toast for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t forget to season with salt and pepper to enhance the taste.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-feta-and-egg-recipes\"><strong>How to Serve this feta and egg recipe</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with crusty whole-grain bread for a hearty breakfast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a fresh garden salad for a light lunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh herbs like dill or parsley for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy alongside roasted vegetables for a colorful dinner plate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with olive oil and a squeeze of lemon for a zesty finish.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and reheating your feta and egg recipe can help you enjoy them later:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the dish to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the dish completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and contents.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 2 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw overnight in the refrigerator if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in the oven at 350°F (175°C) until warmed through.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwave in short intervals, stirring in between.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Check for even heating to maintain texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Does feta cheese go well with eggs?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Feta cheese adds a creamy, tangy flavor that complements the richness of eggs beautifully. Whether scrambled, baked, or in an omelet, feta enhances the dish and provides a delightful contrast to the eggs.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What mixes well with feta?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Feta pairs wonderfully with a variety of ingredients. Fresh herbs like dill and parsley, vegetables such as spinach and tomatoes, and even fruits like watermelon or figs can create delicious combinations. You can also mix it with grains like quinoa or couscous for a hearty meal.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Are feta eggs healthy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, feta eggs can be a healthy option! Eggs are a great source of protein and essential nutrients, while feta cheese provides calcium and healthy fats. Just be mindful of portion sizes, as feta can be high in sodium. Enjoying them in moderation can be part of a balanced diet.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What can feta cheese be eaten with?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Feta cheese is incredibly versatile! It can be enjoyed in salads, on pizzas, in pasta dishes, or as a topping for roasted vegetables. It also works well in dips and spreads, making it a fantastic addition to any cheese board or appetizer platter.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cooking with feta and eggs is a delightful adventure that brings warmth to your kitchen! These recipes are not just simple; they’re a celebration of flavors that will make your taste buds dance. So grab your ingredients, whip up one of these dishes, and enjoy the deliciousness. Trust me, you’ll be smiling with every bite!</p>\n",
